WEBVTT

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.370
Geez, having to work this late...

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:15.390
I heard that Chairman Irie will be checking this place first thing in the morning.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:20.670
Oh yeah, have you heard? They say that this place is haunted.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.900
Yeah, I have.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.590
Apparently, it's pretty famous for it.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.760
Hello, it's Ozawa.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.850
You're planning on going to the hospital today, right?

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:09.780
It's beautiful...

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:10.990
What bad luck...

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:11.970
What?

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.300
...to see your face first thing after waking up.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.810
You ruined my nap.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.320
What have you got in your fridge?

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:43.090
You don't actually live here, right?

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.070
I do have a house, but I rarely go home.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:50.450
But this room belongs to the Film Club, doesn't it?

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:53.070
There is no such club.

00:01:54.230 --> 00:02:00.620
I merely jotted down some random names on the New Club Application form and handed that in.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.880
Are you saying that you lied to the school?

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.010
Isn't that what I just said?

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.260
You're really slow, aren't you?

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.630
What's with the frown?

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.850
Are you mad?

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.350
No, I'm not mad.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:25.690
Of course you aren't. After all, I just told you the truth.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:31.200
More importantly, Miki's waiting for us.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.070
The man who killed you has been arrested,

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.820
so please rest in peace...

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.410
H-Haruka...

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:54.970
What...

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:58.350
Miki, you're awake!

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:05.630
So it really is possible to persuade ghosts from their course of action just by talking to them.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.100
What do you think they are?

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.510
They're not monsters.

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.870
Originally, they were human.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.950
That's true, I guess.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:30.300
It's just my belief, but I think ghosts are clusters of emotions left by those who lost their bodies.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.340
Is that why we can understand each other?

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:40.050
However, if we can't talk sense into them, then we're left with no choice but to exorcise or purify them, right?

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.680
I refuse to acknowledge such methods.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:53.700
I refuse to agree with forcible methods that ignore the ghosts' wishes and either erase or seal them away.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.710
I think I can somehow understand that.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:03.140
And then there are those who have no powers.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:08.230
Those atrocious, self-proclaimed psychics who run bogus businesses for money.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.410
U-Um...

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:15.790
About the 25,000 yen including tax,

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:20.390
I've just started a part-time job, so if you could wait a little longer-

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.170
It has been settled.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.230
What?

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.380
I met her father in the hospital lobby.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:29.880
He paid me then.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.110
Miki's father did?

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.750
I told him I was a psychic who specialized in exorcisms.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.290
He handed me money without being asked.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:43.690
I don't think what you're doing is <i>that much different than those bogus psychics you were ranting about earlier.</i>

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:47.370
In my case, I have actual results to show for it.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:56.510
So, are you involved in any clubs?

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:04.140
I'm in the Orchestra Club. I play the flute.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.040
The next stop is Meisei University.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.650
Meisei University.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:16.400
Our contract ends here.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:33.630
I heard from the manager that you quit.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:39.610
I did, but he begged me to continue working until he finds a replacement.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.030
Is there something you don't like about this job?

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:47.640
Suddenly, I find that I don't need the 25,000 yen including tax anymore.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.900
I'm not quite following...

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:54.000
Oh, right. I'm sorry.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:03.260
Nakahara-san, may I consult you on something?

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:05.920
I'm guessing you want some advice on love?

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:06.680
Oh!

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:12.420
No, it's about a friend of mine.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:15.590
Apparently, she has feelings for someone.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:17.500
What's he like?

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:22.490
He's extremely foul-mouthed and a genius at annoying people.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:29.350
But now that we'll no longer see each other again, I kind of feel sad...

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:34.350
Or at least that's what she told me.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.990
Welcome!

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.620
Well, please call me once you've decided.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:50.540
I'll be quick.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:51.570
Wait there.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.510
It's work-related. Come back later.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:06:59.740
Of course.

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:02.180
Kunimatsu, you too.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.930
I understand.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:07.610
Please accept my apologies.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:14.440
However, he seems to like you.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:16.650
Really?

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:19.440
He's never expressed his real feelings to anyone.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.690
You idiot!

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:22.400
A fox's curse?

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.070
That's just nonsense!

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:25.900
A fox's curse?

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:31.010
We have two fox shrines in the city; one in the east and one in the west.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.730
The shrine in the west is the Kagitsuka Fox Shrine,

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:36.340
and the one in the east is-

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:38.430
The Tamatsuka Fox Shrine, right?

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.800
I pass it on my way home.

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:48.420
The chairman bought the whole area and plans to move the Tamatsuka Fox Shrine

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:52.290
to the Kagitsuka Fox Shrine and erect a new building in its place.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:56.810
However, the development has been facing one problem after another.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.820
Although no one's actually mentioned it,

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:04.630
it's rumored that this is because of the curse of the shrine's god, the fox.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:37.100
Miss, are you all right?

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.360
I-I'm sorry.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.760
Y-Your eye...

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:50.210
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:52.720
Understood.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.080
Just watch me.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.830
I'm sure you'll be very pleased.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.590
I'm looking forward to it.

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:05.670
Are you Saitou-san's father?

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:09.320
No, but we're related.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.840
I'm his mother's brother.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.760
So basically, I'm his uncle.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:16.060
Ah, that explains it.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.610
I've heard all about you from Yakumo.

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:21.770
I see, so you're Haruka-chan.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:24.150
What an amazing coincidence, right?

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:28.320
Buddha's fate has no coincidences, only necessity.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:35.330
I'm positive that Buddha tied our fates together so that we'd meet today.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:41.670
More importantly, where did you say you saw a ghost?

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:43.180
Right over there.

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:48.100
I guess there are times when even normal people can see ghosts without the red eye.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:54.220
Supposedly, ghosts can be seen by normal people if certain conditions are met.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:57.290
Well? Do you see anything?

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:01.000
I guess I can show you the truth.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:07.860
And that's how it is.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:10.990
Why would you do something like that?

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:18.990
Yakumo has been all alone and has suffered much, all because of his left eye.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:23.500
I wished to experience his hardships.

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.010
Isshin-san...

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:31.400
I've heard that he hardly goes home.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.980
He sees ghosts whether he wants to or not.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.930
It's a part of his biological make-up.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.270
Do you know what that means?

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:42.680
This place...

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:49.110
That's right. This is a temple, so a lot of ghosts are naturally drawn here.

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:54.030
To him, this is not a place where he can feel at home.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.800
Yakumo, you're home.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.170
Uncle, I'm borrowing this book.

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:06.210
Of course. I don't mind.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.410
Nao's his cousin.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:18.600
Come now, Nao, say hello to our guest.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.100
Good evening.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.360
You're Nao-chan, right?

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:30.820
What's wrong?

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:34.320
Your words won't reach her.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:37.330
Is she deaf?

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.510
But she has great intuition.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:46.840
She can sense what others are thinking even though she can't communicate verbally.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:57.160
It seems like Nao likes Haruka-chan too.

00:11:57.160 --> 00:12:00.350
How about we all have tea together?

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:12.860
Since Yakumo can see more than most people, he's become perverse

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:16.510
and can no longer honestly express his own feelings.

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:21.370
He may not look like it, but he's a kind boy.

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:30.500
You should ask Yakumo about what you saw at Tamatsuka Fox Shrine.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:33.250
But would he listen to me?

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:40.430
He might complain, but it's in his nature not to ignore things like that.

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:44.330
In that case, I will. Thank you.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:52.440
So, she's the girl who said that Yakumo's eyes are beautiful.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.390
Assistant manager, you seem to be in a good mood today.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:09.120
What?

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:13.590
Oh, my car's finally back from being repaired.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.480
Oh, that's great news.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:30.480
Are you okay?

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.230
Oh, it's you.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:35.040
Are you alone?

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.490
Where's Kunimatsu-san?

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:41.210
There are times when I want to think over things by myself.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.540
Anyway, can you pick that up for me?

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:50.380
This is...

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:52.630
What's wrong with that ema?

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:57.590
When I was looking at this the other day, I saw a ghost.

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:59.130
A ghost, eh?

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:06.640
It was of a lady wearing a beautiful kimono and a fox's mask.

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:09.500
A fox's mask...

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:20.740
Life really <i>is</i>  cruel.

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:26.810
Only when your time is near do you see a vague picture of the truth.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:33.290
Neither money, status, nor fame are important.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:39.300
It's important to be honest to yourself and live life so that you'll have no regrets.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.050
Irie-san...

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:46.880
The ghost you saw is probably...

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.610
Why are you here?

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.770
Who are you?

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:10.810
I'm Saitou Yakumo.

00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:14.920
I'm investigating this area at the request of someone who saw a ghost.

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:16.670
You're investigating this area?

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:21.080
It's true that a ghost lives here,

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:26.670
but what just happened is completely unrelated to that ghost.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:33.950
Because ghosts are merely clusters of emotions.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:37.440
They cannot create any physical phenomena.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:42.700
There's an electrical gadget underneath the scaffolding that utilizes a motor.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.200
The lights contained a tiny amount of gunpowder,

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:49.160
and the laughing voices emitted from speakers hidden in the bushes.

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:53.710
Everything is wired to that shed.

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:05.550
Kunimatsu-san!

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:08.770
Chairman, I am terribly sorry.

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:13.790
Haruka-san, I'm sorry for placing you in danger too.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.190
I am very sorry.

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:17.440
You...

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:23.590
I object to developing on this land.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:29.830
Which is why you faked a curse to try and stop the development.

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:31.380
Yes.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:37.080
Chairman-No, let me call you Tecchan, just like the old days.

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:41.340
Hey, Tecchan, let's bring an end to this.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:47.470
There's nothing that will bring Kuniko-san back to life.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:51.970
Kunimatsu, I've decided.

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:54.470
So, you're going to elope with her, eh?

00:16:56.890 --> 00:17:01.230
We both live in different worlds. That's why...

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.710
this is the only thing we <i>can</i> do.

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:10.870
Take good care of her, Tecchan.

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:13.020
Of course.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:20.630
But it didn't work out well.

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:25.900
The night before, he asked a young worker to relay a message to her.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:30.950
He asked him to tell her, "Wait for me at the fox shrine in the west."

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:35.550
But she was told to wait at the other shrine.

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.390
So they both...

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:41.190
Tecchan waited at the fox shrine in the west,

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:47.490
and Kuniko-san waited here, the fox shrine in the east.

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:52.730
I realized right away,

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:58.410
but men had to be strong back then.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:03.650
Furthermore, our worlds were too far apart.

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:10.670
And because of that, I stayed where I was. I waited for her to come to me.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:14.390
It was just stupid stubbornness.

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:19.270
A year later, she married a man of her parents' choice.

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:26.170
However, she developed tuberculosis and died six months after giving birth to her first child.

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:30.610
Back then, if I'd been more honest with myself,

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:33.570
she might-

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:35.660
Irie-san...

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:39.950
I doubt that I have much time left.

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:44.580
I wanted to free myself from my stupid past

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:47.120
by merging the Tamatsuka Fox Shrine with the Kagitsuka Fox Shrine.

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:49.930
There's no need for that.

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:51.680
Huh?

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:55.950
I can see ghosts.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:57.930
Don't tell me...

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:10.840
Her ghost is still waiting for you over there.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:24.360
Wait... for me...

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:30.840
I'll... be right there...

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:42.850
Kuniko-san...

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:53.110
I'm really sorry.

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:59.370
I wanted to see you.

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:18.940
Her name is Masaoka Kimie.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:21.140
She's the one who asked for my help.

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:29.820
She read her grandmother's diary, visited Tamatsuka Fox Shrine, and saw the ghost.

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:31.780
I see...

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:35.870
So? Why are you here?

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:39.990
I just thought I'd drop by and say hi.

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:42.750
Who asked you to drop by?

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:45.350
No one asked me to drop by.

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:53.520
But after seeing Irie-san, I figured I should be more honest with myself.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.690
I don't get what you're saying.

00:20:56.130 --> 00:21:00.630
What does that have to do with you coming here?

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:02.580
You don't need to understand.

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:15.240
These are all the girls who fit the requirements to become the vessel for my daughter's ghost.

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:20.850
Let's have a toast, Sensei.

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:23.780
To your daughter's revival,

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:28.410
and to the few remaining days of their lives.
